# Large intermediate / cache / raw-download files (over GitHub's 100MB hard
# limit, or just too bulky to bundle). None are unique results: each is
# either reproducible by rerunning the named script against the tracked
# input matrices, or a static public database download. Contact the
# corresponding author for a copy if rerunning isn't practical.

# 2.4GB full 26,169x26,169 gene-gene correlation matrix (protected ComBat).
# Reproduce: 06_PCNWA/combat_protected/scripts/save_full_correlation_matrix_compact.R
06_PCNWA/combat_protected/results/full_gene_correlation_protected_ComBat_dist.rds

# 1.9-0.7GB each: cached anchor-gene correlation matrices (4 base conditions).
# Reproduce: 06_PCNWA/network_robustness/01_cache_anchor_correlations.R
06_PCNWA/network_robustness/01_cached_correlations/

# 416MB/379MB/26MB: raw STRING v12.0 database downloads (static, not
# generated by any script here). Re-download from https://string-db.org
# (organism taxid 29760) or request a copy from the corresponding author.
06_PCNWA/string-db/raw_data/

# 106MB: per-condition mean-variance matrix (exploratory).
# Reproduce: 01_QC_and_Filtering/Batch_effects/exploratory_material/Heteroscedasticity_check_full_grid.R
01_QC_and_Filtering/Batch_effects/exploratory_material/Mean_variance_per_condition_byMatrix.csv

# 97MB: per-gene per-contrast old-vs-new (historical vs. canonical DESeq2) comparison.
# Reproduce: 02_Normalization_and_DGEA/comparison_of_DESeq2_and_ttest/scripts/build_old_vs_new_comparison.R
02_Normalization_and_DGEA/comparison_of_DESeq2_and_ttest/results/DGEA_OldVsNew_perGene_perContrast_comparison.csv

# 76MB: pure-noise AED negative-control draws, all genotypes/timepoints.
# Reproduce: 03_AED/analysis/combat_protected/scripts/AED_noise_negative_control.R
03_AED/analysis/combat_protected/tables/noise_test/noise_negcontrol_all_genotypes_all_timepoints.csv

# 54MB: leave-one-out sensitivity, full per-gene evidence dump.
